<title>SPAIN: IFC issues equity-linked 19 bln pesetas bonds.</title>
<headline>IFC issues equity-linked 19 bln pesetas bonds.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The international Finance Corporation (IFC) is issuing 19 billion pesetas in a five and half year equity-linked matador bond, said Deutsche Morgan Grenfell acting as book runner and lead manager.</p>
<p>The issue is divided in seven tranches, and it is linked to five different share indices, MIB-30, CAC-40, Dax, Ibex-35, FTSE-100.</p>
<p>The coupon is not regular, but varies between 4.30 percent and 4.65 percent as does the maturity date, from October 11, 2002 to October 18 2002.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
